{"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/init(realm:asURI:pat:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/asURI","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/pat","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger\/realm"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configured "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WWW-Authenticate: UMA"},{"type":"text","text":" challenge emitter (CONTRACT.md §20.3, emit half)."}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/UmaChallenger"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UmaChallenger"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Hand one to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamGuards\/requireAccess(_:resource:scope:umaChallenge:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and a denial stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"being a bare 403: the guard mints a fresh permission ticket for the pair the caller lacked and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attaches it to the thrown ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so the framework adapter can return it as a header and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a UMA-aware client knows where to go for authority instead of only being told “no”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Opt-in, and deliberately so."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Emitting a challenge means minting a credential — a wire call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the Protection API, and a live ticket, produced on a path the caller did not explicitly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. A guard that did that on every denial by default would turn each unauthorized request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"into a Protection API call, which is a denial-of-service amplifier pointed at your own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization server. So it happens only where an application asked for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Failure is not escalation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If minting fails — the PAT expired, the Protection API is down,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the resource declares none of the requested scopes — the denial still surfaces as an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthzError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" without a challenge. A caller who was going to be refused is refused either way;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"letting a Protection API outage turn a deny into a 503 would hand the outage a second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"consequence, and letting it turn into an allow would be a security bug."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UmaChallenger","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13UmaChallengerV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UmaChallenger","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure"},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"c